### Palengke Online API requests (VS Code REST Client: click "Send Request" above each one)
@api = http://localhost:4000/api

### Health check
GET {{api}}/health

### Categories
GET {{api}}/categories

### Products: first page (8 per page)
GET {{api}}/products

### Search + category + price range + sort
GET {{api}}/products?search=rice&category_id=4&min_price=100&sort=price_asc

### One category's products
GET {{api}}/categories/2/products

### One product
GET {{api}}/products/1

### Log in as a seller (copy the token into @token below)
# @name login
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "maria@example.com", "password": "Seller123" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### Who am I?
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### My products (seller)
GET {{api}}/seller/products
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Add a product (seller)
# @name created
POST {{api}}/products
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Talong (1 kg)", "price": 70, "stock": 10, "category_id": 1, "description": "Eggplant from Batangas." }

### Add a product WITH a photo (multipart/form-data; the server renames the file to a UUID)
# @name withPhoto
POST {{api}}/products
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=PalengkeBoundary

--PalengkeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="name"

Talong with photo (1 kg)
--PalengkeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="price"

72
--PalengkeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="stock"

6
--PalengkeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="category_id"

1
--PalengkeBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="sample-photo.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./sample-photo.jpg
--PalengkeBoundary--

### Delete the product with the photo (its UUID file is deleted too)
DELETE {{api}}/products/{{withPhoto.response.body.data.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Edit it (seller, own product)
PUT {{api}}/products/{{created.response.body.data.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Talong (1 kg)", "price": 75, "stock": 8, "category_id": 1, "description": "Eggplant from Batangas." }

### Delete it (seller, own product)
DELETE {{api}}/products/{{created.response.body.data.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Error check: Maria edits Pedro's product -> 403
PUT {{api}}/products/3
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Ampalaya (1 kg)", "price": 1, "stock": 1, "category_id": 1 }

### Error check: register with bad data -> 422 with errors per field
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "J", "email": "juan@example.com", "password": "short", "role": "admin" }

### Log out (the token stops working)
POST {{api}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ===== Seller: search, filter and pages =====
GET {{api}}/seller/products?search=rice&stock=in&sort=name&page=1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Seller: inventory totals
GET {{api}}/seller/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ===== Customer: cart and orders (log in as Juan first) =====
# @name customerLogin
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "juan@example.com", "password": "Customer123" }

###
@customerToken = {{customerLogin.response.body.token}}

### See the cart
GET {{api}}/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Add 2 of product 1 (adds to the quantity already in the cart)
POST {{api}}/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "product_id": 1, "quantity": 2 }

### Change the quantity of product 1 to 3
PUT {{api}}/cart/1
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 3 }

### Remove product 1 from the cart
DELETE {{api}}/cart/1
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Checkout: turns the cart into an order (add something to the cart first)
POST {{api}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "address": "Blk 5 Lot 12 Mabini St., Lipa City", "notes": "Please call when you are outside." }

### My orders, newest first
GET {{api}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### One order
GET {{api}}/orders/1
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

